c(14, "§3.1 table (verbatim); §3.1", "data-caveat", "Prioritised unions (verbatim): " + table("## 3.1 The prioritised picture", 0) + " — six findings carry the corpus: delight 73.80%, emotional use 13.60%, reliability (defect_any 36.00%, cant_use_app 17.60%, concentrated in E4), light monetisation friction 12.20%, requests from engaged users 17.20% at 4.70★, language 3.20%; negative_any 262 (52.40%, 3.50★).", "n/a", "mixed", "praise_any 369; outcome_any 135 (27.00%, 4.71★); money_any 91 (18.20%, 3.79★); defect_any 180; request_any 86 (4.70★); lost_user_signal 27 (5.40%, 2.33★)", "none", "table", "generalisable", ["11575242405"], "", "")

c(15, "§3.2 table (verbatim); §3.2", "insight", "What people value (verbatim): " + table("## 3.2 What people value", 0) + " — cute is the first word (PRAISE_CUTE 157, 31.40%: 'my bunny passed away recently and I kind of enjoy taking care of the rabbit in the app'); the loop motivates (GAMIFICATION 76, 4.68★: 'even the fun of growing a sprout in the sunlight'); all in one (23 — one deleted separate to-do, goal and diary apps); design (43); inclusion (2: 'the gender field has an undecided option besides female and male; I found that thoughtful'); free and ad-light (FREE_GENEROUS 14, NO_ADS 6: 'as long as ads don't appear, I'll keep using it').", "cute character + reward loop", "praise", "CUTE 157 / 31.40% / 4.50★; GAMIFICATION 76 / 4.68★; ALL_IN_ONE 23; DESIGN_UI 43; INCLUSIVE 2; FREE_GENEROUS 14; NO_ADS 6", "build-free", "High-priority", "generalisable", ["12221992891", "7062422745", "12713833538", "7844208245", "10444659530"], "", "")

c(16, "§3.3 table (verbatim); §3.3", "feature", "Outcomes, the letters and AI (verbatim): " + table("## 3.3 Outcomes", 0) + " — OUT_HABIT_BUILT 97 (19.40%, 4.68★); OUT_EMOTIONAL_SUPPORT 64 (12.80%, 4.84★: 'when I read the letter I felt those feelings slowly drift away'); the letter is known to be AI and valued anyway ('Even if it's ai, they've always been really well done'; '누군가는 인공지능의 답변이기에 무의미하다고 느낄 수도 있겠지만'); limits and defects — PAYWALL_LETTERS_AI 8 ('it's sad I only get replies twice a week', 2★; 'you have to pay for the AI letter, but the app didn't warn you and it just stops', 2★), BUG_LETTER_AI 9 ('it skips asking about the ChatGPT letter'; Dr. Eddy named the wrong author), AI_CONTENT_DISLIKE 1 ('very cliche answers'); Dr. Eddy praised 6 times (2023-08 → 2024-10: 'it helps me with my homework'; 'a rabbit who listens to your problems') and later asked about as removed.", "AI support letter (limited free), Dr. Eddy chat (status unclear)", "praise", "SUPPORT_LETTER 70 / 14.00% / 4.69★; EMOTIONAL_SUPPORT 64 / 4.84★; PAYWALL_LETTERS_AI 8; BUG_LETTER_AI 9; DR_EDDY 6", "build-paid", "High-priority", "generalisable", ["9597261099", "12390183328", "11180689493", "11353456949", "12542235186", "10871827849", "10594910174", "12348613423", "13083050847", "11838028848", "11714582957", "10597118888", "14161345933"], "", "the AI reply is the paid hook and the emotional core at once")

c(17, "§3.4 table (verbatim); §3.4", "audience", "Uses and segments (verbatim): " + table("## 3.4 Uses and segments", 0) + " — mental health (USE_MENTAL_HEALTH 16, 4.75★: ADHD 4, autism, depression 2, anxiety 2, crisis 2); students and children (SEG_STUDENT_MINOR 13: 'I am a high school student and it has helped me cope'; a 4+ app with 14+ sign-up — '앱이4세 이상인데 14세이상 가입이니 조금 당황스러워요'; an elementary-schooler asking whether it keeps charging); switchers (SEG_TRIED_MANY 23, 4.91★ — the second-highest mean of any code with ten or more); long-term users (SEG_LONG_TENURE 16, 3.56★, 11 of 16 in E4 reporting the blank diary); it is read as a game (META_CALLS_IT_GAME 6).", "n/a", "mixed", "USE_MENTAL_HEALTH 16 / 4.75★; STUDENT_MINOR 13; TRIED_MANY 23 / 4.91★; LONG_TENURE 16 / 3.56★; AGE_GATE 1", "none", "High-priority", "generalisable", ["12007216026", "12151980131", "13303553647", "11366311382", "8775129558", "10308816687"], "", "")

c(18, "§3.5 table (verbatim); §3.5", "must-never-break", "Reliability (verbatim): " + table("## 3.5 Reliability", 0) + " — 'new bugs seem to appear with every update, so I'm thinking of switching apps' (3★); an earlier launch cluster March–April 2023 ('it breaks every like 3-4 days'); BUG_UPDATE_LOOP 7 — a forced update that cannot be installed (2022, Feb–Mar 2025, Mar–Apr 2026); core loop: BUG_ROUTINE_TRACKING 20, BUG_REWARDS 15 (2.80★), BUG_WIDGET 15 (routine order reversed in the widget; in July 2025 the widget disappeared for a paying user), BUG_REMINDERS 6; DATA_LOSS 11 (2.91★: 'after updating, all my diary entries disappeared'; 'It lost all my fragments. I had dozens.'); BUG_PERFORMANCE 17 (loading circles, lag, overheating); friction that is not a bug: UX_CLUNKY 18, REDESIGN_DISLIKE 4, FEATURE_BLOAT 3 ('I wish I could hide the room-decorating tab'; one left for a more minimal app — 'I've decided to leave the bunny behind'), ONBOARDING_LONG 1 ('endless questions and promotions').", "frequent regressions across releases", "complaint", "defect_any 180 / 36.00% / 3.33★; core_loop_defect 51 / 10.20%; LAUNCH_LOAD 26 / 2.85★; UPDATE_LOOP 7; ROUTINE_TRACKING 20; REWARDS 15; WIDGET 15; DATA_LOSS 11; PERFORMANCE 17; UX_CLUNKY 18; FEATURE_BLOAT 3", "must-never-break", "High-priority", "generalisable", ["14086081070", "9736739746", "9849991980", "11758713945", "12898347981", "10782496310", "14060686801", "10793137161", "8411737665", "11188145228"], "", "")

c(19, "§3.6 table (verbatim); §3.6", "monetization", "Free tier, prices and ads (verbatim): " + table("## 3.6 Free tier", 0) + " — routine cap (FREE_LIMIT_ROUTINES 12: 'I'll just use another app', 1★; in 2021 the cap was on records — 'it's like don't use it unless you pay'); price (PRICE_TOO_HIGH 10, eight in Korea: '₩39,000 seems too expensive', 5★; 'about $60/yr' with an ad on every task completion; PRICE_FAIR 2: 'honestly isn't that bad at 7.99'); subscription format (WANT_ONE_TIME_PURCHASE 6: 'a subscription feels like slavery'; 'どうしても買い切りが欲しい'); price not visible (PRICE_OPAQUE 8: 'services that don't show the price clearly aren't very trustworthy'); slow economy (REWARD_ECONOMY_SLOW 7: 'It is so hard to get the coins') and paid cosmetics (PAYWALL_COSMETICS 4: 'A bit greedy').", "8-routine cap; ₩55,000 / $59.99 yearly; no lifetime; paid Ultimate cosmetics", "complaint", "FREE_LIMIT_ROUTINES 12; PRICE_TOO_HIGH 10 (8 KR); PRICE_FAIR 2; WANT_ONE_TIME 6; PRICE_OPAQUE 8; REWARD_ECONOMY_SLOW 7; PAYWALL_COSMETICS 4", "undecided", "High-priority", "generalisable", ["8981491200", "6903629058", "9904411482", "12509850218", "11381876235", "9936992932", "12555565779", "12122537449", "12518317305", "12354142663"], "", "")

c(20, "§3.7 table (verbatim); §3.7", "monetization", "Paid users and billing (verbatim): " + table("## 3.7 Paid users", 0) + " — PAID_EXPLICIT 27 (5.40%, 3.67★), PAID_SATISFIED 12, PAID_NOT_UNLOCKED 4, PAID_REGRET 4; billing complaints rare — BILL_UNEXPECTED_CHARGE 2 ('I started a 7-day free trial and was charged ₩4,400'; 'suddenly ₩55,000 for a year was charged').", "subscription with 7-day trial", "mixed", "PAID_EXPLICIT 27 / 3.67★; SATISFIED 12; NOT_UNLOCKED 4; REGRET 4; BILL_UNEXPECTED 2", "none", "High-priority", "generalisable", ["12619312572", "11872679326"], "", "")

c(21, "§3.8", "market", "Language and localisation — U:language_gap 16 (3.20%, mean 4.38★): reviewers who want to use the app, not reviewers leaving; 2022 Korean-only ('Will it be available in English?' while the listing already claimed English); 2024–2026 Chinese ('希望增加繁體中文！') and Vietnamese; partial translation — Korean in the gacha and store, untranslated Japanese strings, no am/pm time format; six Korean-language reviews from outside Korea.", "EN + KO; partial", "complaint", "language_gap 16 / 3.20% / 4.38★", "do", "Very strong", "generalisable", ["8997324225", "13458634572", "14113680514", "14273717431", "10523193240"], "", "")

c(22, "§3.9 table (verbatim); §3.9", "feature", "Requests (verbatim): " + table("## 3.9 Requests", 0) + " — U:request_any 86 (17.20%, 4.70★), 65 five-star; platforms — REQ_IPAD_WATCH_MAC 15, all Korean ('I want to buy premium but hesitate because I use my iPad a lot'; a paying user mainly uses Todo Mate, 'cheaper and works with Apple Watch'); scheduling — REQ_FLEX_SCHEDULE 10 (every N days, weekly counts, reps '10 planks a day', recurring deadlines, a pomodoro timer, a later day boundary: 'not getting carrots for tasks done after midnight kills motivation'); character and room — REQ_CUSTOMISE_CHARACTER 14 at 5.00★ (outfits, poses, rooms, seasonal themes); diary — REQ_DIARY_FEATURES 10 (photos, more letters, more moods, memos; a payer: 'letters are unlimited, which is good, but I can only write one a day'); widgets 9, social 5 (shipped Jan 2026), sort order 5, font size 3.", "iPhone only; daily scheduling; 1 diary/day", "complaint", "request_any 86 / 17.20% / 4.70★; IPAD_WATCH_MAC 15 (KR); FLEX_SCHEDULE 10; CUSTOMISE_CHARACTER 14 / 5.00★; DIARY_FEATURES 10; WIDGET 9; SOCIAL 5; SORT 5; FONT 3", "none", "High-priority", "generalisable", ["8775133101", "10332206320", "11780393009", "12518607166", "9782795049", "11116476663", "11031708917"], "", "")

c(23, "§3.10 table (verbatim); §3.10", "insight", "Support, trust and churn (verbatim): " + table("## 3.10 Support", 0) + " — SUPPORT_QUESTION 43 (8.60%, 4.37★: how to collect coins, join events, cancel, change language, fix errors); support failures 15 (UNRESPONSIVE 6, UNREACHABLE_INAPP 6, NEGLECT_PERCEIVED 7: 'it's starting to feel like the app is being neglected'); churn — U:lost_user_signal 27 (5.40%, 2.33★): CHURN_STATED 13, CHURN_RISK 11, ACCOUNT_DELETE 4, reasons ads (3), bugs (2), the paywall (3), minimalism (1), a paid feature that never unlocked (1); fraud language almost absent (SCAM_LANGUAGE 2); competitors named 8 — Todo Mate, me+, Study Bunny, Finch, Duolingo (as a nag to avoid: 'it's not gonna harass you like Duolingo', and as a widget model), Animal Crossing (price anchor), iPhone built-ins.", "n/a", "mixed", "SUPPORT_QUESTION 43; support_negative 15; lost_user_signal 27 / 2.33★; SCAM_LANGUAGE 2; COMP_NAMED_APP 8", "none", "High-priority", "generalisable", ["14156911446", "13852438902", "12354142663", "13115443882", "13741115225", "10332206320"], "", "")

